{% extends "tool_layout" %}
{% import "icons" as icons %}

{% block tool %}
<section class="panel panel-pad tool-panel" aria-labelledby="gen-heading">
    <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-3" id="gen-heading">Your new password</h2>
    <div class="input-group input-group-lg">
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="password">Generated password</label>
        <input type="text" class="form-control font-monospace generated-password" id="password" readonly spellcheck="false">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-quiet" id="password-gen" title="Generate a new password"
            aria-label="Generate a new password">{{ icons.icon("refresh") }}</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-accent" data-copy="password">{{ icons.icon("copy") }} Copy</button>
    </div>
    <p class="small text-secondary mt-2 mb-0" id="password-entropy"></p>

    <hr class="panel-divider my-4">

    <div class="row g-3 align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-8">
            <label for="password-len" class="field-label">Length: <span class="text-secondary fw-normal"
                    id="pass-len-display"></span></label>
            <input type="range" class="form-range" min="8" max="128" value="16" id="password-len">
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="form-check form-switch">
                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" role="switch" id="use-special" checked>
                <label class="form-check-label small" for="use-special">Include symbols (!@#$%^&amp;* etc.)</label>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}

{% block about %}
<h2 class="h4">How the passwords are made</h2>
<p>Each character is picked at random from upper and lower case letters and digits, plus symbols if
    you include them. The randomness comes from your browser's cryptographically secure random number
    generator (<code>crypto.getRandomValues</code>), the same source used for encryption keys, and every
    character is equally likely. The password is created on your device and is never saved or sent
    anywhere.</p>

<h2 class="h4">How long should a password be?</h2>
<p>Length matters more than anything else. The figure under the password shows its <strong>entropy</strong>:
    how many guesses an attacker would need, written as a power of two. Each extra bit doubles the work.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>16 characters</strong> (about 95 bits, or 103 with symbols) is far beyond what can be
        brute-forced and is a good default for accounts.</li>
    <li><strong>20 or more</strong> is a good choice for password manager master passwords, encryption keys
        and Wi-Fi networks.</li>
    <li>Leave symbols out if a site doesn't accept them, and add a few characters of length instead.</li>
</ul>
<p>Use a different password for every account, and keep them in a password manager. To share one with
    someone, send it in a <a href="/">self-destructing encrypted paste</a> rather than in plain chat or
    email.</p>
{% endblock %}
